# This repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but CI and the Docker
# image both run on Linux. Without this file, whether a checked-out Dockerfile
# or workflow has CRLF line endings depends on each teammate's git config —
# and a stray \r inside a `RUN ... \` continuation or a `run: |` block is a
# shell error that only appears on someone else's machine.
#
# Let git normalise text to LF in the repository...
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...and pin LF in the working copy for everything Linux executes or parses.
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers stay CRLF.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
